  "notes": "とても is a common adverb meaning \"very\" or \"extremely.\" It's polite and versatile, suitable for most situations.\n\nUSAGE:\n- Modifies adjectives: とても⟦{大|おお}きい→大きい：00335_ookii⟧ (very big)\n- Modifies verbs: とても⟦{疲|つか}れた→疲れる：00901_tsukareru⟧ (very tired)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦すごく→すごく：18751_sugoku⟧: very (more casual, emphatic)\n- ⟦{大変|たいへん}→大変：00594_taihen⟧: very, terribly (can imply difficulty)\n- ⟦{非常|ひじょう}→非常：01598_hijou⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: extremely (formal)\n- ⟦とっても→とっても：noentry⟧: very (casual variant of とても)\n\nNEGATIVE PATTERN:\nとても + negative = \"cannot possibly\"\n- とても⟦{食|た}べられない→食べる：00396_taberu⟧: I can't possibly eat it\n- とても⟦{無理|むり}→無理：01558_muri⟧⟦だ→だ：09496_da⟧: It's absolutely impossible\n\nREGISTER:\nとても is neutral and appropriate for both spoken and written Japanese.",
